<LegalPage title="Accessibility" lede="We want everyone to be able to use our website, including people who use screen readers, keyboards or other assistive tools.">
  <h2>Our goal</h2>
  <p>We aim to follow the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA. We keep working on this, and some parts may not be perfect yet.</p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every page has a "Skip to content" link for keyboard users.</li>
    <li>Menus, buttons and forms can be used with a keyboard, and focus is visible.</li>
    <li>Photos have text descriptions, and decorative images are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li>Text is high contrast and the layout adapts to phones, tablets and zoom.</li>
    <li>We respect your device setting to reduce motion.</li>
    <li>We write in plain, easy words.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limits</h2>
  <p>Some older blog posts, and third-party tools such as online booking, may not fully meet these standards. We are working with those providers to improve them.</p>

  <h2>Need help or found a problem?</h2>
  <p>Tell us and we will help you get the information or service you need, in another way if necessary. Call <a href="tel:+14809639000">480-963-9000</a> or visit our office. Please tell us the page and the problem you ran into.</p>

  <h2>In our office</h2>
  <p>If you need an accommodation for your visit, such as wheelchair access or help with forms, please tell us when you book and we will plan ahead.</p>
</LegalPage>
